title: $:/changenotes/5.5.0/#9986
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* A block element such as `<div>` is no longer wrapped in a paragraph, so a static render and the interactive page no longer disagree about the same source. Across tiddlywiki.com this removes 75 invalid paragraphs and every empty one
* The decision is now taken when the content renders rather than while parsing, so it is also correct for content arriving through a transclusion or a macro, which the parser could not see
* A run mixing text and a block element is split the way a browser splits it, so text either side of the block keeps its paragraph
* `@@.myClass` wrapped around a block now applies the class to that block
* Custom CSS that relied on a `p` selector matching those paragraphs inside core user interface tiddlers may need updating, since the paragraphs are gone
